<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore says 1996 unit labour costs grew 3.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore says 1996 unit labour costs grew 3.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's unit labour cost indes grew 3.5 percent in 1996, the Ministry of Trade and Industry said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The rise came after three consecutive years of decline, the ministry said.</p>
<p>It said: &quot;Nominal and real wage growth grew at a faster pace than productivity growth in 1996.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
